  "publication_date": "2023-08-31",
  "pse": {
    "problem": "Unbalanced and varying datasets in participant nodes lead to precision reduction in federated learning models",
    "solution_function": "The system selects specific participant nodes with relevant data classes based on their data distribution information, then applies data preprocessing techniques to balance the data before federated averaging is performed",
    "solution_structure": "The system consists of a coordinator node and multiple participant nodes. Each participant node has local storage for data and processing capabilities. The coordinator node communicates with all participant nodes and aggregates model updates from them.",
    "solution_implementation": "1. Coordinator node obtains data distribution information of each participant node based on a target feature. 2. Coordinator node selects relevant participant nodes for training based on the target class and data distribution information. 3. Selected participant nodes preprocess their data to balance it. 4. Each participant node trains the AI model using its preprocessed data and sends updated model parameters/gradient values to the coordinator node. 5. Coordinator node aggregates the updates using federated averaging algorithm.",
    "effect": "Improved precision of federated learning models by accounting for unbalanced and varying datasets in participant nodes"
  },
